Git stores repository directory and last Process.
initialize: use current directory and no last process.
directory: get repository directory; directory: path sets it and returns self.
lastProcess: return the most recent process, including output, status and exitCode.
run: arguments starts git directly with the supplied argument array in directory, waits, and returns the Process even on failure.
checked: arguments returns output on zero exit; otherwise signals directory, command, exit code and captured output.
status, diff, stagedDiff, head, branch, remotes, log: return checked Git query output.
fetch: remote fetches a remote.
add: paths stages only supplied paths, after the end-of-options delimiter.
commit: message commits the staged changes with the exact message argument.
push: remote branch: name pushes the named branch to the remote, without force.
SSH authentication
    Keep per-object enabled flag, identity file, agent socket and config file.
    useSSH enables batch SSH; useDefaultAuth restores normal Git authentication.
    sshIdentityFile:, sshAgent:, sshConfigFile: set or clear overrides and enable SSH.
    sshCommand builds the SSH command with separately quoted paths.
    run prepends the per-invocation Git SSH command override when enabled.
    remote: url: and remote: pushURL: set repository remote URLs.
    checkAuth: probes remote refs and signals failure through checked:.
